  "content": {
    "id": "p52-g96-99-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Find the value(s) of $k$ for the following to have equal roots.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p52-g96-99-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$kx^2-6x+k=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$k=\\pm3$.",
          "worked": "Equal roots require $\\Delta=0$ and $k\\ne0$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}(-6)^2-4(k)(k)&=0\\\\36-4k^2&=0\\\\k^2&=9\\\\k&=\\pm3.\\end{align*}$$\n\nBoth values have $k\\ne0$, so both give equal roots.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p52-g96-99-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$x^2-(k+4)x+9=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$k=-10$ or $k=2$.",
          "worked": "For equal roots, $\\Delta=0$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}[-(k+4)]^2-4(1)(9)&=0\\\\(k+4)^2&=36\\\\k+4&=\\pm6\\\\k&=-10\\text{ or }2.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe coefficient of $x^2$ is $1$ for both values.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p52-g96-99-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$2kx^2+2(k-2)x-3=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p52-q98-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "No real value of ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "k",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " gives equal roots.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p52-q98-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\Delta=4\\big((k+1)^2+3\\big)>0",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "; at ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "k=0",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " the equation is linear.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "For $k\\ne0$, find the discriminant.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Delta&=[2(k-2)]^2-4(2k)(-3)\\\\\\Delta&=4(k-2)^2+24k\\\\\\Delta&=4(k^2+2k+4)\\\\\\Delta&=4\\big((k+1)^2+3\\big)>0.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThus $\\Delta$ cannot be zero, so the quadratic cannot have equal roots.\n\nAt $k=0$, the equation is $-4x-3=0$, which is linear and has no double root.\n\nHence no real value of $k$ gives equal roots.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "p52-g96-99-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$kx^2-3kx+3=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p52-q99-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "k=\\frac{4}{3}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " only.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p52-q99-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Set ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\Delta=3k(3k-4)=0",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "; reject ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "k=0",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " because it gives ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "3=0",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Equal roots require $\\Delta=0$ and $k\\ne0$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}(-3k)^2-4(k)(3)&=0\\\\9k^2-12k&=0\\\\3k(3k-4)&=0\\\\k&=0\\text{ or }\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{align*}$$\n\nAt $k=0$, the equation becomes $3=0$, so it has no roots.\n\nHence $k=\\frac{4}{3}$ only.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 54
      }
    ]
  },
